  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "ambient: one chord held for the whole piece, a bright pad holding over it in long swells, and a far bell now and then above 2 kHz - no drums, no pulse",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "The harmony is a pedal: one chord, never moved. Over it a sustained part asked for bright and long-held - the formant pad preferred, the wide saw, the grain and the wave pads admitted - holds sixteen beats at a time, wide-voiced, re-entering every eight bars; a distant bell on a bright keyboard sounds once every three to five bars. Plays under the Ambient tile's spell, where the drums are off; the row asks for no drums and claims no rhythm. The shimmer above 4 kHz is the composer's own at the floating place (GA6) and not a lead a row can ask for.",
